# The image is built from an allowlist: only the platform's code goes into the build context. Run
# history, worker memory, Teams, workspaces, credentials, prompts, exports, benchmarks, tests and
# node_modules built on another OS never reach it (deleting them in a later layer would still ship
# them in an earlier one). docs/CLOUD_DEPLOYMENT.md.
*

!deploy/entrypoint.sh
!deploy/egress-firewall.sh

!mcp/package.json
!mcp/package-lock.json
!mcp/*.mjs
!browser-adapter/package.json
!browser-adapter/package-lock.json
!browser-adapter/server.mjs
!figma-reader/*.mjs
!builder-adapter/*.mjs

!worker-ui/assets/*.png
!worker-ui/*.html
!worker-ui/worker-instructions.md
!worker-ui/worker-efficiency.md
# Every console module by pattern, not by name: a named list went stale when the console gained
# modules (catalog, integrations, workerdef, …) and the image's consoles couldn't start.
!worker-ui/*.mjs
# The integrations registry: manifests, schemas, order and the release lock (data, no state). The
# whole folder: with the legacy builder, "integrations/*/*.json" doesn't reach the subfolders.
!worker-ui/integrations
